    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of assessing Direct Air Capture's (DAC) economic viability and strategic role for climate stabilization, given polarizing debates and the lack of comprehensive, model-based analyses that compare it with a full suite of other mitigation options under stringent climate policies.",
    "method": "This paper uses the WITCH energy-economy-climate model, implementing a detailed techno-economic specification for Direct Air Capture (DAC), to assess its long-term deployment, economic impacts, and role in achieving stringent climate stabilization targets under various global policy scenarios.",
    "task": "The task is to assess the role and long-term prospects of direct air capture (DAC) of CO2 for achieving stringent climate stabilization using the WITCH energy-economy-climate model.",
